338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 100 0 R
/T (The program starts by showing the guidelines and reading the player's name. A level begins only while at least one lifeline remains. Inside a level the player's text is first converted to an integer and checked against the allowed range; both checks send control straight back to the input step, so invalid entries never reduce the lifelines. A valid guess is compared with the secret number: an exact match clears the level and moves on, while any other guess prints a hint, removes a lifeline and repeats the loop. When lifelines reach zero the game ends, the secret number is revealed and the summary is printed. Finally main\(\) asks whether to play again and either restarts the session or exits.)
/E (The program starts by showing the guidelines and reading the player's name. A level begins only while at least one lifeline remains. Inside a level the player's text is first converted to an integer and checked against the allowed range; both checks send control straight back to the input step, so invalid entries never reduce the lifelines. A valid guess is compared with the secret number: an exact match clears the level and moves on, while any other guess prints a hint, removes a lifeline and repeats the loop. When lifelines reach zero the game ends, the secret number is revealed and the summary is printed. Finally main\(\) asks whether to play again and either restarts the session or exits.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
