/T (The Number Guessing Game was designed, implemented and tested successfully. It meets every requirement of Problem Statement No. 89: the computer picks a secret number between 1 and 100, the player gets five attempts, hints are given after each wrong guess, and boundary values, invalid input and exhausted lifelines are all handled correctly. The extended five-level design with shared lifelines and a session record makes the game more engaging while still using only fundamental Python constructs.)
/E (The Number Guessing Game was designed, implemented and tested successfully. It meets every requirement of Problem Statement No. 89: the computer picks a secret number between 1 and 100, the player gets five attempts, hints are given after each wrong guess, and boundary values, invalid input and exhausted lifelines are all handled correctly. The extended five-level design with shared lifelines and a session record makes the game more engaging while still using only fundamental Python constructs.)
